<title>FRANCE: New York is top Jan-Mch ex-Paris cargo destination.</title>
<headline>New York is top Jan-Mch ex-Paris cargo destination.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in first quarter 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in January-March 1997, with the percentage change on January-March 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>	City		 Tonnes	   Pct change</p>
<p>	New York	   8,681	    down  3.2</p>
<p>	Chicago	    6,735		up 11.4</p>
<p>	Tokyo		6,291	    down 13.9</p>
<p>	Hong Kong	  5,340		up  2.3</p>
<p>	Sao Paulo	  3,550		up 49.8</p>
<p>	Montreal	   3,384	    down  9.5</p>
<p>	Mexico City	3,223		up 11.8</p>
<p>	Singapore	  2,854		up 52.9</p>
<p>	Los Angeles	2,612	    down  7.6</p>
<p>	Dubai		2,005	    down 14.1</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
